@startuml
' Figure 22.6  The supersession chain
' Reading order: left to right. A record is written as head; a newer
' observation on the same subject and scope supersedes it, and the old
' version stays readable to the desk. A write against a stale head, or
' an older observation, is refused. Deletion ends any version. From
' memory.store.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
hide empty description
state Head <<knowledge>>
state Superseded <<knowledge>>
state Refused <<knowledge>>
state Deleted <<verified>>
[*] --> Head : Written
Head --> Superseded : Newer observation
Head --> Refused : Stale head or older
Head --> Deleted : Erasure, tombstone
Superseded --> Deleted : Erasure, tombstone
Deleted --> [*]
@enduml
